  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "A new triplestore to support core relationships",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "management in the core Fedora repository will be",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "developed for the following reasons:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "make core repository not dependent on kowari",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "due to kowari instability issues and high memory",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "requirements, we must ensure that the core repository",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "is not vulnerable to these things",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "basic relationship management is something we can",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "achieve with a simpler triplestore.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "basic relationship management must be contained",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "within the contect of a Fedora API-M transaction. ",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "Right now, the kowari solution entails Fedora writing",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "triples to a buffer that is outside the context of the",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "Fedora API-M transaction, thus it cannot be guaranteed",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "that such triples have successfully been written to the",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "triplestore from the buffer by the time the Fedora",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "API-M transaction is completed. ",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "For these and other reason, a new triplestore is being",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "developed using relational database technology. The",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "design of this triplestore is based on mapped triple",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "tables (thus MTP). It will hold all the same",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "information currently in the Resource Index model. ",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "Initially, it will support SPO queries.",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "This will be an alternative configuration for the",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "Resource Index in the core Fedora. It will still be",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "possible to configure kowari as the triplestore. ",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "At the same time, we are moving forward with designs to",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "have a Resource Index service that can be outside the",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "core Fedora repository. The idea is to have simpler",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "and more tranasction-savvy relationship management at",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "the core of Fedora, then be able to replicate the",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "managed triples from the core to triplestore outside",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "the repository (the Resource Index service) via",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "messaging. The motivation here is to make the external",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "service be where more semantic web activities happen",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "(outside of the core repository). The base information",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "from the repository can be enriched in the service (add",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "information from other ontologies, add other kinds of",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "relationships, whatever.) Then, full blown",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "capabilities such as inferencing, can be done via the",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "type": "hardBreak"
          },
          {
           "text": "service without bogging down the core repository.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    }
   ],
